[0.010, "o", "\r\n==============================================================================\r\nQ: Did our signups fall from last month?\r\n==============================================================================\r\n\r\nConfidence: medium\r\nTook 57s over 4 steps, 19,760 tokens, 13 observations gathered, 8 cited\r\n\r\nANSWER\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  No, signups have not actually fallen: the apparent 62% drop in August is an artifact of August's data ending on the 12th, not a real decline.  [ga4.compare_periods 95ef26d2, posthog.event_trend c93bcf5b]\r\n  The daily signup rate has stayed flat at roughly 150-163 per day through all of July and the first 12 days of August.  [posthog.event_trend c93bcf5b]\r\n\r\nFINDINGS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  Monthly totals look like a drop only because August has fewer days of data  (medium)\r\n    - GA4 sessions for August (partial, 12 days) are down 61.9% versus July's full 31 days, and"]
[0.000, "o", " conversions are down 61.81%, but this comparison itself notes the two windows are not comparable since August only has 12 days of data against July's 31.  [ga4.compare_periods 95ef26d2]\r\n    - The PostHog weekly signup series shows a similar apparent drop in the week of Aug 10, but that week's bucket only covers data through Aug 12, not the full week.  [posthog.event_trend c66d1f81, posthog.event_trend c93bcf5b]\r\n    - Looking at the daily signup counts, the rate holds steady at roughly 149-163 per day across all of July and the first 12 days of August, with no decline at the daily level.  [posthog.event_trend c93bcf5b]\r\n    - GA4 daily sessions for August 1-12 are similarly flat, ranging 150-165 sessions per day with no downward trend.  [ga4.get_sessions ee9e06e9]\r\n\r\nCHARTS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  user signed up over time\r\n  value\r\n    value              |▅█████▁|  459 → 1,110\r\n                        2026-06-29 … 2026-08-10\r\n\r\n  u"]
[0.000, "o", "ser signed up over time\r\n  value\r\n    value              |▄▁█▇▅▃█▅▇▇▅▄▅▄▂▃▇▁▁▅▃▅▄▃█▂▄▂▅▃▃▇▃▅█▂▁▃▇▆▃▃▂|  149 → 164\r\n                        2026-07-01 … 2026-08-12\r\n\r\n  sessions over time\r\n  sessions\r\n    sessions           |▂▁▁▂▆▁▁▄▂█▁▄|  150 → 165\r\n                        2026-08-01 … 2026-08-12\r\n\r\n\r\nRISKS AND CAVEATS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - PostHog and GA4 data both stop at 2026-08-12, so the second half of August cannot be verified; if a real decline began after Aug 12 it would not appear in this data.\r\n  - A Slack message from a team member perceived signups as down and speculated about a pricing redesign, but no commit history or decision record could be found to confirm a pricing change occurred, so this perception could not be independently verified either way.\r\n  - 2 claim(s) go beyond their evidence and are retained with red"]
[0.001, "o", "uced confidence rather than removed, because the rest of each one holds. What the check found:\r\n- executive_summary[0]: The 61.9% drop figure comes from sessions/conversions data explained as a partial-month artifact, and the signup event trend confirms steady daily counts through Aug 12, but the ev\r\n- findings[0].claims[2]: All daily values fall within 149-164, with one value (164 on 7/25) exceeding the claimed 149-163 range, but otherwise the steady, non-declining pattern is confirmed.\r\n\r\nDATA QUALITY\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - August 2026 data in both GA4 and PostHog ends at 2026-08-12, giving only 12 of 31 days; any total-based month-over-month comparison will appear as a large decline purely due to missing days, not an actual drop in the underlying rate.\r\n  - 3 of the 8 cited observation(s) returned no results (github.commits, slack.find_decision). Conclusions resting on them describe what was not found, which is not the same as what does not exis"]
[0.000, "o", "t.\r\n\r\nSOURCES\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  95ef26d2  ga4.compare_periods  eval://ga4__compare_periods\r\n  ee9e06e9  ga4.get_sessions  eval://ga4__get_sessions\r\n  26fe7ded  github.commits  eval://github__commits\r\n  c16d5402  github.commits  eval://github__commits\r\n  c66d1f81  posthog.event_trend  eval://posthog__event_trend\r\n  c93bcf5b  posthog.event_trend  eval://posthog__event_trend\r\n  8a084856  slack.find_decision  eval://slack__find_decision\r\n  0fb20441  slack.search_messages  eval://slack__search_messages\r\n"]
